Full review comments:

- [P1] Exclude future native identities beyond the three study issues — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/r/fm17_opponent_freeze.R:70-74
  The exclusion list comes from `fixtures`, which the input client populates only for 26098, 26101 and 26102. For a 26098 forecast, native identities from future issues 26099 and 26100 are therefore absent. If one of those matches appears in history with an incorrectly early date, shared admission treats it as an ordinary `MATCH:` row and admits its label. Supply an independently bound exclusion roster covering intervening future issues, rather than deriving it from the evaluation subset. This violates the exact-identity exclusion requirement in [AGENTS.md:114](AGENTS.md#L114).

- [P2] Reconcile group weighting policies with the declared preparation — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/packages/beidan/inst/python/beidan_backend/opponent_goals.py:144-149
  Verification checks that each context independently replays and references the admission, but never checks that its weighting policy follows `prepared['policy']` or that its partition is the prescribed team/venue group. I replaced all four valid recent-blend contexts with independently valid expanding-equal contexts, updated their exported ledgers/receipts, and verification accepted them while the declared policy still specified alpha 0.5 and 12-match activation. Reconstruct the expected groups and shared weighting policies from admitted facts and compare them, so valid but unrelated contexts cannot authorize different fitting weights. See [AGENTS.md:135–137](AGENTS.md#L135-L137).

- [P2] Rebuild team columns after removing disconnected components — /home/drwho1985/workspace/algotradinglife/beijing-lot/packages/beidan/R/opponent_goals.R:51-53
  When unrelated disconnected teams exist, their observations are removed but `teams` still includes them, leaving zero attack/defence columns in the design. Glmnet rescales `penalty.factor` to sum to the number of columns, so these unused columns change the effective ridge penalty on retained teams. Consequently, adding an entirely disconnected network changes target lambdas despite identical retained observations and weights; a local two-versus-twelve-team reproduction changed predicted means. Recompute `teams`, attack and defence indices from the selected component before constructing the design.
